<urn:beads-cache:finding:RQA9-001> triage:ownerAssessment "{\"finding\": {\"correlation\": \"Same actual occurrence as independent rust-qa-agent RQA9-001; retain this ID, not a duplicate FTQ ID.\", \"evidence\": \"Exact b7de8e9879503353879c500edacf12a6832d709d run41776396362 Windows job126397662727, raw rust-qa-hosted-c2-windows.log:1950-1965: first read-only negative records kill/reap5.005945s and original500ms observation; next busy-persistence child output contains only running1test and test name; assertion1084 fails worker operation did not run; store33passed1failed, exit101. Source schedule.rs:1056-1095 starts an owned child, finishes at5s, checks timeout/cleanup receipt/under7s, then checks post-call marker and500ms-expiry output. Busy path:861-919 includes database preparation, worker call, stall marker and timed completion observation. Shared store tree6286e1f33ae881d92e7acaf95852c4010ab82cbc, source blobd30f281677d56389285827faabeb4d8aace48758 and helper blobd312b5608d5bd50511647227cf865938219e3efb match C1/C2/adbc exactly.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-store/src/schedule.rs\", \"id\": \"RQA9-001\", \"issue\": \"Actual frozen C2 Windows required CI fails the shared-store negative fixture because its busy-persistence child reaches the five-second supervisor deadline without recording the required post-worker-call stalled-cleanup receipt. The parent has killed/reaped the child, but that occurrence does not qualify the intended busy-persistence stalled-join path. This is a concrete failed test observation requiring investigation; the underlying cause and whether it is a fixture race or store-path fault are unresolved.\", \"limits\": \"Timing classification describes the observed watchdog/receipt failure only. Logs do not locate the child at timeout or prove host scheduling, SQLite malfunction, missing product cancellation, orphaning, or a newly introduced source regression. Missing receipt does not prove the operation never began or returned. This is separate